        "content": "<p>alexcrichton opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15256\">issue #15256</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If a global initializer traps during instantiation, serializing the resulting core dump panics in debug builds when a later global has a non-nullable reference type:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">module</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array</span> <span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">global</span> <span class=\"nv\">$g0</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array.new_default</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mf\">0x7fffffff)</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">global</span> <span class=\"nv\">$g1</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">ref</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">array.new_default</span> <span class=\"nv\">$a</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">))))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gc</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coredump</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">repro</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">thread</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">main</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">panicked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">crates</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">src</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">runtime</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">externals</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">global</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rs</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">237</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">21</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"nc\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">non</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">nullable</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">we</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">better</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">non</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">null</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reference</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is sort of a more general problem where instances are left in a half-baked state on trapping during instantiation which means that we don't have a great way to reflect over them in a core dump. At the same time, however, reflecting over a core dump is exactly what you'd want in such a situation.</p>\n<p>My guess is that this is probably also a problem for the guest-debug feature where inspecting globals on a trap might get wonky if everything's not fully initialized.</p>\n</blockquote>",
